<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20899" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρᾰχύτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>, ἡ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shortness</i>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆκος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				283c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελέτης βραχύτητι</span> with
				<i>shortness</i> of practice, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.138
			</span></i>; <i>narrowness, deficiency</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ βραχύτητος γνώμης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.42
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>smallness</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ βάθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					354a18
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>shortness</i> of a syllable, in prosody, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				400c
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1456b32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.947e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				1.100
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>scantiness</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ὄντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Or.</u>
					62.59
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>shallowness</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαλάττης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Scyl.
					112
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b> Rhet., <i>use
				of a condensed</i> or <i>allusive expression</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Trypho
				<u>Trop.</u>
				p.202
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i></div>
